> On 08.02.2012 16:21, Karl Garrison wrote:
>> I searched the code, and couldn't find anything like this, but if
>> there any way in the code to determine of a piece of armor has been
>> previously worn by the player?
>
> As far as I can tell, no. For items on the floor you could look at 
> obj->invlet to see if it was ever in the inventory, but to track 
> previously worn you'd need a new field in struct obj.

You could also check to see if the player knows the item's enchantment.
For armour, this implies either that it's been previously worn, or that
it's been identified with a scroll of identify or similar effect. (I
guess you could also look at the rknown field to tell the two situations
apart. I'm not convinced that this would be 100% reliable in determining
if the armour had been worn in the past, but it must be reasonably
close.)

